          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "veṇu first meant \"a bamboo, a reed\" in the Rigveda and later \"a flute\" (MW). MW thinks it probably comes from the root √ve \"weave\", but CDIAL 12096 finds its connections unclear, so its origin is uncertain."
            }
          ]
